<article class="env-remark" id="04K4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04K4">Remark <span data-tag="04K4">66.19.11</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $x \in |X|$. We claim that for any pair of geometric points $\overline{x}$ and $\overline{x}'$ lying over $x$ the stalk functors are isomorphic. By definition of $|X|$ we can find a third geometric point $\overline{x}''$ so that there exists a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \overline{x}'' \ar[r] \ar[d] \ar[rd]^{\overline{x}''} &  \overline{x}' \ar[d]^{\overline{x}'} \\  \overline{x} \ar[r]^{\overline{x}} &  X. }  \]
</div>
  <p> Since the stalk functor $\mathcal{F} \mapsto \mathcal{F}_{\overline{x}}$ is given by pullback along the morphism $\overline{x}$ (and similarly for the others) we conclude by functoriality of pullbacks. </p>
</article>